/-!
# The original binary half-path actor and its literal cyclic two-core

The same source geometry and opposite roots identify every binary-midpoint
halfactor as a dihedral group of order six times a power of two. The
canonical quotient kernel is exactly the cyclic subgroup generated by the
cube of the product of the two selected root involutions. All quotient,
torus, reflection-class and eight-midpoint perfectness data are retained.
A bound on the binary two-part and its central reflection correction remain
separate mathematical duties; neither is an input to this producer.
-/

public noncomputable section
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false
open Subgroup Theory.GroupTheory RankTwoAmalgam SimpleGraph SimpleGraph.Walk
open Theory.GroupTheory.AmalgamGraph Subgroup.CosetGeometry.RankTwo
open Theory.GroupTheory.WeakBNPair.RegularTree
open CFSG.Quasithin.ChapterF.Section01.SourceRecognition.DGS85.ApartmentExchange
